Title: Dal Tadka (Restaurant Style)

Channel: vegrecipesofindia.com

Linked recipe blog structured data (schema.org Recipe JSON-LD) — prefer this for method text when it has instructions:

{
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Dal Tadka (Restaurant Style)",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Dassana Amit"
  },
  "description": "This restaurant-style Dal Tadka recipe is a smooth and creamy lentil dish made with pigeon pea lentils (tur dal), onions, tomatoes and herbs, finished with a tempering of spices like cumin, garlic, dried red chillies, asafoetida and red chilli powder. The dhungar method gives the dal a subtle smoky flavor. It is best served with steamed basmati rice or enjoyed with roti or paratha.",
  "datePublished": "2025-03-17T12:50:33+00:00",
  "image": [
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/dal-tadka-3.jpg",
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/dal-tadka-3-500x500.jpg",
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/dal-tadka-3-500x375.jpg",
    "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/dal-tadka-3-480x270.jpg"
  ],
  "video": {
    "name": "Dal Tadka",
    "description": "Dal Tadka is a popular Indian lentil dish made with arhar dal or tuvar dal (husked &amp; split pigeon pea lentils) or masoor dal (husked &amp; split red lentils). This recipe is of restaurant style dal tadka with has smokey flavors and aroma.",
    "thumbnailUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/thumbs/os763iYF-720.jpg",
    "contentUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/videos/os763iYF.mp4",
    "uploadDate": "2020-09-08T00:00:00+00:00",
    "@type": "VideoObject"
  },
  "recipeYield": [
    "4"
  ],
  "prepTime": "PT20M",
  "cookTime": "PT10M",
  "totalTime": "PT30M",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "1 cup or (200 grams)  tuvar dal",
    "1 to 2  green chilies (or serrano peppers - chopped or slit lengthwise)",
    "½  cup onions  (- chopped)",
    "1 cup tomatoes  (- finely chopped)",
    "1 teaspoon ginger (- finely chopped)",
    "½  teaspoon turmeric powder ((ground turmeric))",
    "½   teaspoon garam masala",
    "1 pinch asafoetida ((hing), optional)",
    "2.5 cups water (- for pressure cooking)",
    "1 tablespoon light cream (or low fat cream, optional)",
    "2 tablespoons coriander leaves (- chopped, (cilantro))",
    "salt  (as required)",
    "3 tablespoon oil (or 3 tablespoon ghee (clarified butter))",
    "1 teaspoon cumin seeds",
    "5 to 6  garlic cloves (- finely chopped, small to medium-sized)",
    "2 to 3  dry red chilies (- broken and seeds removed)",
    "1 generous pinch of asafoetida ((hing), optional)",
    "1 teaspoon kasuri methi (- crushed, (dry fenugreek leaves), optional)",
    "½ teaspoon kashmiri chilli powder (or cayenne pepper or paprika)",
    "1 to 2 tablespoons coriander leaves (- chopped (cilantro))",
    "1 small piece of natural charcoal",
    "¼ teaspoon oil (or ghee (clarified butter))"
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Cook lentils",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Thoroughly rinse tuvar dal (tur dal) in water. Add them to a 3-litre stovetop pressure cooker.You can also cook the lentils in a pot. Soak the lentils for an hour or two before you cook them in a pot adding water as needed.If cooking in a pot, you could add about 3 to 3.5 cups of water.",
          "name": "Thoroughly rinse tuvar dal (tur dal) in water. Add them to a 3-litre stovetop pressure cooker.You can also cook the lentils in a pot. Soak the lentils for an hour or two before you cook them in a pot adding water as needed.If cooking in a pot, you could add about 3 to 3.5 cups of water.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add the chopped onions, finely chopped tomatoes, chopped green chillies and finely chopped ginger.",
          "name": "Add the chopped onions, finely chopped tomatoes, chopped green chillies and finely chopped ginger.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Pour 2.5 cups of water into the pressure cooker.",
          "name": "Pour 2.5 cups of water into the pressure cooker.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add turmeric powder and asafoetida (hing). Mix well.",
          "name": "Add turmeric powder and asafoetida (hing). Mix well.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Pressure cook the lentils on medium to medium-high heat for about 7 to 8 whistles (about 8 to 10 minutes), or until the lentils become soft and creamy.",
          "name": "Pressure cook the lentils on medium to medium-high heat for about 7 to 8 whistles (about 8 to 10 minutes), or until the lentils become soft and creamy.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Let the pressure drop naturally in the cooker and then only open the lid. Check the lentils to see if they have cooked thoroughly and softened.",
          "name": "Let the pressure drop naturally in the cooker and then only open the lid. Check the lentils to see if they have cooked thoroughly and softened.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-5"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Mash the cooked lentils with a wired whisk or with a spoon and set aside.",
          "name": "Mash the cooked lentils with a wired whisk or with a spoon and set aside.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-6"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "If the consistency looks thick, add about ½ to 1 cup water (depending on the thickness) to get a medium consistency. Mix again and on a low to medium-low heat simmer dal for 3 to 4 minutes.",
          "name": "If the consistency looks thick, add about ½ to 1 cup water (depending on the thickness) to get a medium consistency. Mix again and on a low to medium-low heat simmer dal for 3 to 4 minutes.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-7"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Once the desired consistency is reached, add the light cream or low-fat cream (optional), garam masala powder, chopped coriander leaves (cilantro) and salt to taste. Turn off the the heat.",
          "name": "Once the desired consistency is reached, add the light cream or low-fat cream (optional), garam masala powder, chopped coriander leaves (cilantro) and salt to taste. Turn off the the heat.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-8"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Mix well so that everything combines to an even consistency. Taste and adjust salt before adding tadka.",
          "name": "Mix well so that everything combines to an even consistency. Taste and adjust salt before adding tadka.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-0-9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Smoke lentils using dhungar method (optional)",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "To get the smoky flavor of burnt charcoal like you would in a restaurant, you&#039;ll want to follow the dhungar method. Using tongs, place a small piece of charcoal on a grill pan like shown in the photo below. Burn the charcoal until it becomes red hot. Please be sure to use natural charcoal for this method, avoiding anything that has a flame accelerant added. Note that this is an optional step - you can proceed directly to the tempering method.",
          "name": "To get the smoky flavor of burnt charcoal like you would in a restaurant, you&#039;ll want to follow the dhungar method. Using tongs, place a small piece of charcoal on a grill pan like shown in the photo below. Burn the charcoal until it becomes red hot. Please be sure to use natural charcoal for this method, avoiding anything that has a flame accelerant added. Note that this is an optional step - you can proceed directly to the tempering method.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-1-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Place the red hot charcoal in a small steel bowl. You can also use a halved hollow onion instead of the bowl.",
          "name": "Place the red hot charcoal in a small steel bowl. You can also use a halved hollow onion instead of the bowl.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-1-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Pour about ¼ teaspoon of oil or ghee on the charcoal. You will see fumes emanating as soon as you pour oil or ghee on the hot charcoal.",
          "name": "Pour about ¼ teaspoon of oil or ghee on the charcoal. You will see fumes emanating as soon as you pour oil or ghee on the hot charcoal.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-1-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Place this bowl on the dal.",
          "name": "Place this bowl on the dal.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-1-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Cover the cooker or pot with a lid and let the dal get infused. Only smoke for 1 to 2 minutes. Do not keep for a long time, or you&#039;ll risk making the dal taste bitter. Remove the bowl carefully with the help of tongs and cover the cooker with a lid. Set aside.",
          "name": "Cover the cooker or pot with a lid and let the dal get infused. Only smoke for 1 to 2 minutes. Do not keep for a long time, or you&#039;ll risk making the dal taste bitter. Remove the bowl carefully with the help of tongs and cover the cooker with a lid. Set aside.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-1-4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Make the tempering (tadka or chaunk)",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Next, heat oil or ghee (clarified butter) in a small pan over low or medium-low heat.",
          "name": "Next, heat oil or ghee (clarified butter) in a small pan over low or medium-low heat.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-2-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "First, add the cumin seeds and crackle them. The cumin should get fried and not be raw, but be careful not burn them.",
          "name": "First, add the cumin seeds and crackle them. The cumin should get fried and not be raw, but be careful not burn them.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-2-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Next add the dry red chilies, asafoetida, and finely chopped garlic. Let the garlic brown lightly and the red chilies change color. Do not burn the garlic.",
          "name": "Next add the dry red chilies, asafoetida, and finely chopped garlic. Let the garlic brown lightly and the red chilies change color. Do not burn the garlic.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-2-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Lastly, add the crushed kasuri methi (dried fenugreek leaves) and kashmiri red chili powder or cayenne pepper. Mix well and turn off the stove.",
          "name": "Lastly, add the crushed kasuri methi (dried fenugreek leaves) and kashmiri red chili powder or cayenne pepper. Mix well and turn off the stove.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-2-3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Make Dal Tadka",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Pour entire tempering mixture along with the oil or ghee into the prepared dal.",
          "name": "Pour entire tempering mixture along with the oil or ghee into the prepared dal.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-3-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "You can either mix the dal with tempering, or serve the dal tadka with the tempering on top of it.",
          "name": "You can either mix the dal with tempering, or serve the dal tadka with the tempering on top of it.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-3-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Garnish with coriander leaves.",
          "name": "Garnish with coriander leaves.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-3-2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Serving Suggestions",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Serve Dal Tadka hot with steamed basmati rice or jeera rice (cumin rice).",
          "name": "Serve Dal Tadka hot with steamed basmati rice or jeera rice (cumin rice).",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-4-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "You can also enjoy the dal with roti or paratha.",
          "name": "You can also enjoy the dal with roti or paratha.",
          "url": "https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/restaurant-style-dal-tadka/#wprm-recipe-139406-step-4-1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
